  "statement": "For $f(x)=x^{3}-3x$, find its stationary points and state their nature, and find the equation of the tangent at $x=2$.",
  "solution": "$f'(x)=3x^{2}-3=3(x-1)(x+1)$, zero at $x=\\\\pm1$. $f''(x)=6x$: at $x=1$, $f''>0$ so minimum $f(1)=-2$; at $x=-1$, $f''<0$ so maximum $f(-1)=2$. At $x=2$, $f=2$ and $f'=9$, so tangent $y-2=9(x-2)$, i.e. $y=9x-16$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
